  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Alliance for Change Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will focus on Building Unbiased HIV and Mental Health Response for LGBTIQ+ Rightsholders and to meet health equity. Themain objective is to reduce incidences of violation of health rights and gender injustice that perpetuate the HIV pandemicand implication of mental illness for LGBTIQ as a result of HIV positive. The project will contribute to increased access to inclusive HIV treatment and sexual health right services and mental healthcare, reduction of viral load suppression, HIV transmission and increase prevention.  YACK will conduct monthly outreach clinical and behavioural campaigns to support retention in care and medication adherence with the objective of increasing retention on ARTs among LGBTIQ+. To address stigma and discrimination and promote health equality, we will train health care providers on friendly SRHR and HIV treatment and prevention services, health rights and gender justice. We will enhance peer navigation with the objective of to linking peer LGBTIQ+ living with HIVto equal treatment by conducting HIV counselling Services HTS. This will result to increased up-take on ART, PEP and PrEP among the community LGBTIQ. The project will ensure holistic HIV treatment for LGBTIQ+ with HIV by facilitating monthly psychosocialand health behavioural support for LGBTIQ+ to improve retention to decline social isolation.  We will be intentional in identifying, engaging or re-engaging LGBTIQ+ with HIV who are not on HIV treatment or not virally suppressed this will be achieved thorough establishment of referrals networks, engage ARTs defaulters among LGBTIQ+ and re-initiate them on ARTs treatment. We expect increased knowledge on HIV prevention and reduced HIV-related stigma through behaviour changer campaigns and community awarenesson access to services and HIV stigma and discrimination We willpartner with NASCOP/ LVCT to acquire in-kind donation HIV Self-Test kits, condoms &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; lubricants, PEP and PrEP during the sessions for HTS testing with service providers. The project will prioritise the safety LGBTIQQ+ and their privacy and confidentiality and visits all activities and conversation that could expose them to potentially life-threatening attention.</narrative>
  </description>
